module v2.workflow.floor_preparation_split

import std.types { Bool, Int, List, Present, Absent, String }
import std.algebra { length, list_push }
import std.list { distinct_by_key }
import std.measure { Millisecond, millisecond, millisecond_count }
import extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io { Filesystem }

// THE TIME CARRIER. Every duration in this authority -- the split's two sides and their total, a
// module's cost, the in-force phase reading, a parse variant's amount, an entry's resolve time, the
// attributed top -- is a `std.measure` Millisecond. Producer digits are wrapped the moment they are
// parsed (`floor_preparation_amount`, the `[resolve]` classifier), so no bare duration integer is ever
// stored, compared, or carried out. The reader surface the claims module uses
// (`floor_preparation_split_preparation_ms` and siblings) returns the carrier's COUNT, named for the
// unit it counts; `floor_preparation_line_ms` and the per-module readers do the same, because they are
// readings, not carriers.
fn floor_preparation_ms_zero() -> Millisecond { millisecond(count: 0) }
fn floor_preparation_ms_of(count: Int) -> Millisecond { millisecond(count: count) }
fn floor_preparation_ms_add(left: Millisecond, right: Millisecond) -> Millisecond {
  millisecond(count: millisecond_count(left) + millisecond_count(right))
}
fn floor_preparation_ms_count(carrier: Millisecond) -> Int { millisecond_count(carrier) }

// WHERE THE REQUIRED FLOOR'S WALL TIME ACTUALLY GOES, ASKED RATHER THAN BELIEVED.
//
// `gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn` took the witness floor off the merge path because its
// whole-run cost did not fit the fleet beside the build lane, and `gunbc.roadmap
// ci-cost-floor-preparation-cut` is the node that makes it affordable. The row's premise is that the
// CLAIMS WERE NEVER THE EXPENSE -- claim execution is a small fraction of the floor's wall time while
// strict preparation and the reach probes dominate it -- and it names the two candidate repairs:
// reusing resolved-module and reach-probe results across runs, or scoping preparation to a diff's
// closure. That premise travelled as prose. No entry point re-derived it, so the cost decision would
// have been taken against a figure nobody could reproduce -- which is how `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt`'s
// population count rotted three times: prose copied beside its producer and never re-read.
//
// THIS FILE IS THAT ENTRY POINT. It folds the instrument lines one floor-shaped `claim_batch` run
// printed over the committed population, and answers the split at module grain. Ask it:
//
//   gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 \
//     --entry src/v2/workflow/floor_preparation_split.dag \
//     --function floor_preparation_split_report
//
// NOT THE SAME SUBJECT AS `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt`, and the two must not be confused. That file
// folds WHICH enrolled identities the over-cost withholding holds back from published census rows --
// its `floor_cost_debt_population_report` answers "how many identities are withheld, and is that set
// closed". THIS file folds the instrument lines one run printed and answers WHERE THE TIME WENT:
// preparation versus claim execution, at module grain. Neither claims to be the other's measurement,
// and the witness `the_split_fold_is_not_the_cost_debt_fold` refuses if they ever start to. Ask this
// file for the cost split; ask floor_cost_debt for the withheld population. (Ordered by
// royal-newt-240, msg_8712db4a: extend one authority rather than mint a competing one -- and if a
// second is right, say in each what the other covers and this one does not.)
//
// THE CAPTURE IS GENERATED, NEVER TYPED. `floor_preparation_capture`, its provenance twin,
// `floor_preparation_untrimmed_capture`, `floor_preparation_untrimmed_capture_provenance` and
// `floor_preparation_requested_rows` are spliced between the generated-block markers by
// `v2.workflow.floor_preparation_capture_runner`, which reads the phase lines one real `claim_batch
// --claim-run` printed and REFUSES -- on a 0-byte binary, one hashing as the empty string, a sha that
// deviates from the pinned release or from `release-bins.manifest`, an argv missing `--functions`, an
// entry that never reported its witness count, a `[floor-shared-fill]`/`[floor-reach-probe]` pairing
// mismatch, or a FAIL trying to enter the graded capture. The population it enrolled is committed at
// `dag/test/claim/floor/floor_preparation_split_population.txt`. Re-deriving the split needs no fleet
// slot: `--mode fold` recomputes every row from a log you already hold.
//
// The run REFUSES -- the host maps a verdict to an exit code and only `ProcessExit` carries one -- and
// prints the returned String in the refusal, which is the reading. That is the same shape
// `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt::floor_cost_debt_population_report` has and for the same reason: a
// report is not a verdict. The executed witnesses are:
//
//   target/release/claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 \
//     --claim-run --entry dag/test/claim/floor/floor_preparation_split_witness.dag \
//     --functions <the names its header lists>
//
// RELATION TO `v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt`, WHICH IS ADJACENT AND NOT THIS SUBJECT. That file folds
// WHICH IDENTITIES the over-cost withholding mechanism holds, per identity, off published census
// rows; it decides nothing about where a run's wall time is spent and enrols nothing from the phase
// lines. This file folds the run-level phase rows and the per-claim instrument rows into the
// preparation-versus-claim split the affordability decision needs. Neither reads the other's lines,
// and neither quotes the other's figures.
//
// NO WITNESS PINS THE SPLIT TO A MILLISECONDS LITERAL, and that is deliberate: an assertion that the
// preparation total equals a number copied out of this same tree is the change detector
// `gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed` refuses, and it would have to be re-edited on every re-capture.
// What guards the fold is four structural properties, each an executed witness in
// `dag/test/claim/floor/floor_preparation_split_witness.dag`:
//
//   1. CLOSED GRAMMAR -- every tagged line lands in a bucket or the fold REFUSES naming itself, so a
//      phase renamed upstream cannot be silently dropped from the split.
//   2. CONSERVATION -- the split's grand total equals the total an INDEPENDENT fold of the same lines
//      computes, so nothing is double-counted or lost.
//   3. DELETION MARGIN -- removing one costed line from the capture moves the total by exactly that
//      line's own reported cost, which is what makes the figure derived from the lines rather than
//      transcribed into this file.
//   4. CLASSIFICATION CAUSALITY -- the two per-claim rows that report the SAME fill
//      (`[floor-shared-fill]` and `[floor-reach-probe]`) contribute that fill ONCE, and every silent-zero
//      path in the fold refuses instead of reading as zero. `claim_batch` prints the probe row immediately
//      after the fill row under the same condition, repeating the same `fill_cpu_ms`
//      (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/claim_execution.rs:183 and :214 read the same
//      `shared_artifact_fill_cpu`), so counting both would report a preparation figure inflated by every
//      fill -- the same direction as the premise this node is asked about, which is why the classification
//      needs a causal witness and not merely a consistent one. Because a real capture only shows a fill
//      when preparation left the artifact cold, that witness reads a short capture the claims module
//      authors (`floor_preparation_the_fold_bills_the_reach_probe_fill_once`,
//      `floor_preparation_the_fold_refuses_what_it_cannot_read`), alongside
//      `floor_preparation_committed_fill_rows_are_paired` over the world's own rows.
//
// THE CAPTURE IS A TRANSCRIBED INSTRUMENT OUTPUT, DECLARED AS ONE. `gunbc.design_argument::
// how_to_work` rules that the measurement is the producer and that prose quoting a producer's output is
// how a figure rots. The honest form available to a fold over a PAST run is to commit the instrument's
// output verbatim and make the model read the lines, which is what `floor_preparation_capture` holds,
// with the producer, binary sha, tree sha and argv recorded by `floor_preparation_capture_provenance`.
// The capture is reproducible: the command is printed inside the report, the population it enumerated
// is committed at `dag/test/claim/floor/floor_preparation_split_capture_population.json`, and any
// reader can regenerate both the lines and this reading from them.

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE GRAMMAR. The tag set and field names are the ones the captured binary printed, each cited to its
// print site on main, so a token added, renamed or deleted upstream is a refusal with a locus rather
// than a silent reclassification. A `state=` other than `completed` DEMOTES a costed phase row to
// uncosted-and-counted (a started row has no timing field to read); it is never dropped.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

type FloorPreparationCostClass
  = PreparationCost // owed by the run before, or around, any claim executing
  | ClaimExecutionCost // owed by the claim itself
  | NotCostBearing { reason: String } // printed for judgement or census; carries no timing field to read

// WHICH CHOICE OF THE TWO THE ROADMAP OFFERS CAN EVEN REACH A GIVEN PREPARATION COST. A whole-tree
// phase pays for the whole published corpus, so it recurs on a run whose diff touches one file: only
// REUSING RESOLVED-MODULE AND REACH-PROBE RESULTS ACROSS RUNS can stop paying it. An entry-closure phase
// pays for the closure the run's entries union into, so SCOPING PREPARATION TO A DIFF'S CLOSURE cuts it
// by cutting the entries. Read without this dimension the preparation side is one number and the node's
// cost decision would be taken blind; the whole-tree / entry-closure split IS that decision, and it is
// derived from the same lines rather than asserted.
type FloorPreparationScale
  = WholeTreeScale // prints pool_files=/source_files= over the published corpus; recurs whatever the diff is
  | EntryClosureScale // prints entries=/sources= over the run's entry union; falls with the entries

type FloorPreparationPhaseRow {
  phase: String,
  class: FloorPreparationCostClass,
  cost_field: String,
  scale: FloorPreparationScale,
  authority: String,
}

// THE CLOSED PHASE TOKENS, and on which side of the split each one's cost is owed.
data floor_preparation_phase_rows: List<FloorPreparationPhaseRow> = [
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "module-index", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: WholeTreeScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs precompute_whole_tree_published_mock_keys" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "declarer-discovery", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: WholeTreeScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs precompute_whole_tree_published_mock_keys" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "whole-tree-graph-facts", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: WholeTreeScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs precompute_whole_tree_published_mock_keys" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "declarer-closure", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: WholeTreeScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs precompute_whole_tree_published_mock_keys" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "closure-strict-resolve", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: EntryClosureScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs precompute_whole_tree_published_mock_keys (sources= over the entry closure)" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "gate-closure", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: EntryClosureScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs assemble_prepared_subject_from_corpus" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "reference-closure-index", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: EntryClosureScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs build_reference_closure_index" },
  // THE PHASE THIS NODE EXISTS FOR. It reports `cpu_ms` and `wall_ms` for the same build; the fleet
  // carries the WALL clock beside the build lane, so `wall_ms` is the figure charged. The
  // `provenance=built-by-preparation` field on this row is what says preparation found the memo COLD and
  // paid the build -- the quantity cross-run reuse is proposed to stop paying -- and
  // `scope=entry-closure-union` is what says its size is set by the run's ENTRIES, so diff-closure
  // scoping reaches it without any cache at all.
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "bare-reference-edge-index-warm", class: PreparationCost, cost_field: "wall_ms", scale: EntryClosureScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs:1114 provenance=built-by-preparation scope=entry-closure-union" },
  // JUDGEMENT ROWS THAT CARRY NO TIMING FIELD. Counting them as zero would invent a cost; dropping them
  // would lose a line. They are counted, uncosted, and reported in `uncosted_lines`.
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "expr-var-classification", class: NotCostBearing { reason: "prints occurrence census and per-kind counts with no timing field " }, cost_field: "", scale: EntryClosureScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs build_reference_closure_index" },
  FloorPreparationPhaseRow { phase: "reach-differential", class: NotCostBearing { reason: "a merge-group judgement row printed state=deferred_to_merge_group with no timing field (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/reach_base_standings.rs:70)" }, cost_field: "", scale: EntryClosureScale, authority: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/reach_base_standings.rs:70" },
]

fn floor_preparation_phase_row(phase: String) -> Optional<FloorPreparationPhaseRow> {
  fold(floor_preparation_phase_rows, init:  none, f: (acc, row) => if row.phase == phase { Present { value: row } } else { acc })
}

data floor_preparation_phase_tag: String = "[floor-phase]"
data floor_preparation_shared_fill_tag: String = "[floor-shared-fill]"
data floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag: String = "[floor-reach-probe]"
data floor_preparation_resolve_tag: String = "[resolve]"
data floor_preparation_witness_tag: String = "[witness]"
data floor_preparation_pass_prefix: String = "PASS "
data floor_preparation_fail_prefix: String = "FAIL "
data floor_preparation_unknown_tag_cause: String = "a tagged instrument row whose tag this grammar does not know; refused rather than counted as nothing"

// A LINE, AS THE GRAMMAR READS IT. `claim_batch` resolves an entry (printing `[resolve] <path>:
// <ms>ms ...`) and only then runs its claims (printing `[witness]`, and the fill rows), so the module a
// per-claim row belongs to is the entry of the most recent `[resolve]` line. The fold THREADS that
// entry rather than guessing: a per-claim row printed before any `[resolve]` REFUSES, because
// attributing it to no module or to a module invented from its bare function label would both be worse
// than refusing.
type FloorPreparationLine
  = PhaseLine { phase: String, fields: List<String> }
  | EntryResolveLine { entry: String, ms: Millisecond }
  | ClaimLine { tag: String, claim: String, fields: List<String> }
  | VerdictLine { passed: Bool, function: String }
  | UntaggedLine { text: String }
  | RefusedLine { text: String, cause: String }

fn floor_preparation_tokens(line: String) -> List<String> {
  let pushed = fold(split(s: line, delimiter: " "), init:  [], f: (acc, token) =>
    if token == "" {
      acc
    } else {
      concat([token], acc)
    })
  floor_preparation_reverse(pushed)
}

fn floor_preparation_reverse<T>(xs: List<T>) -> List<T> {
  fold(xs, init:  [], f: (acc, x) => concat([x], acc))
}

// Local fold-based count: the shared universal `length` resolves its type argument
// monomorphically per module, so a second element type through it is refused.
fn floor_preparation_count<T>(xs: List<T>) -> Int {
  fold(xs, init: 0, f: (acc, _) => acc + 1)
}

// THE `key=value` ATOMS FOLLOWING A FIXED HEAD TOKEN.
fn floor_preparation_fields_after(line: String, head: String) -> List<String> {
  let pieces = split(s: line, delimiter: head)
  match pieces.skip(n: 1).first() {
    Present { value: rest } => floor_preparation_tokens(rest)
    Absent => []
  }
}

// A `key=value` atom, read by its key. The whole atom is compared first so a key that is a PREFIX of
// another key (`cpu` against `cpu_ms`) cannot be satisfied by the longer one.
fn floor_preparation_field(fields: List<String>, key: String) -> Optional<String> {
  let wanted = concat(key, "=")
  fold(fields, init:  none, f: (acc, field) =>
    if acc != none {
      acc
    } else {
      let pieces = split(s: field, delimiter: "=")
      if pieces.length() < 2 {
        none
      } else {
        match pieces.first() {
          Present { value: k } =>
            if field == wanted || k == key {
              pieces.skip(n: 1).first()
            } else {
              none
            }
          Absent => none
        }
      }
    })
}

// A MONEY FIELD, READ STRICTLY. `parse_int` would happily accept "-47", and accepting that would lift a
// broken counter to its magnitude; and a missing field is NOT a zero, it is the line not telling us.
type FloorPreparationAmount
  = Amount { ms: Millisecond }
  | MissingField { key: String }
  | MalformedValue { key: String, text: String }

fn floor_preparation_ms_field(fields: List<String>, key: String) -> FloorPreparationAmount {
  match floor_preparation_field(fields, key) {
    Absent => MissingField { key: key }
    Present { value: text } => floor_preparation_amount(key: key, text: text)
  }
}

// A FIELD WHOSE VALUE CARRIES ITS UNIT, as `[witness]`'s `cpu=12ms` does. The unit is REQUIRED: a bare
// `12` in that position means the producer changed format, and reading it silently is how a unit
// becomes milliseconds in one release and microseconds in the next.
fn floor_preparation_ms_unit_field(fields: List<String>, key: String) -> FloorPreparationAmount {
  match floor_preparation_field(fields, key) {
    Absent => MissingField { key: key }
    Present { value: text } =>
      match floor_preparation_strip_suffix(text, "ms") {
        Absent => MalformedValue { key: key, text: text }
        Present { value: digits } => floor_preparation_amount(key: key, text: digits)
      }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_amount(key: String, text: String) -> FloorPreparationAmount {
  match parse_int(s: text) {
    Absent => MalformedValue { key: key, text: text }
    Present { value: n } => if n < 0 { MalformedValue { key: key, text: text } } else { Amount { ms: floor_preparation_ms_of(n) } }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_amount_ms(amount: FloorPreparationAmount) -> Int {
  match amount {
    Amount { ms: n } => floor_preparation_ms_count(n)
    MissingField { key: _ } => 0
    MalformedValue { key: _, text: _ } => 0
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_starts_with(text: String, prefix: String) -> Bool {
  let pieces = split(s: text, delimiter: prefix)
  pieces.length() > 1 && pieces.first() == Present { value: "" }
}

fn floor_preparation_after_prefix(text: String, prefix: String) -> String {
  let pieces = split(s: text, delimiter: prefix)
  match pieces.skip(n: 1).first() {
    Present { value: rest } => rest
    Absent => ""
  }
}

// `text` must END with `suffix`; Absent says it does not, which is a format deviation and not a zero.
fn floor_preparation_strip_suffix(text: String, suffix: String) -> Optional<String> {
  let pieces = split(s: text, delimiter: suffix)
  if pieces.length() == 2 {
    match pieces.skip(n: 1).first() {
      Present { value: "" } => pieces.first()
      _ => none
    }
  } else {
    none
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_strip_prefix(text: String, prefix: String) -> String {
  let pieces = split(s: text, delimiter: prefix)
  if pieces.length() == 2 && pieces.first() == Present { value: "" } {
    match pieces.skip(n: 1).first() {
      Present { value: rest } => rest
      Absent => text
    }
  } else {
    text
  }
}

// THE MODULE IDENTITY AN ENTRY PATH NAMES. The rule is: the source-root prefix and the `.dag` suffix
// removed, separators dotted. For a claim module under `dag/` that IS its declared identity
// (`dag/test/claim/emitter_variant_tag_reference_witness.dag` becomes
// `test.claim.emitter_variant_tag_reference_witness`), which is what puts the entry-resolve rows and
// the per-claim rows in ONE key space instead of two.
fn floor_preparation_module_of_path(path: String) -> String {
  let without_root = if floor_preparation_starts_with(path, "dag/") {
    floor_preparation_strip_prefix(path, "dag/")
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(path, "src/") {
    floor_preparation_strip_prefix(path, "src/")
  } else {
    path
  }
  let without_suffix = match floor_preparation_strip_suffix(without_root, ".dag") {
    Present { value: v } => v
    Absent => without_root
  }
  floor_preparation_join_dots(without_suffix)
}

fn floor_preparation_join_dots(path: String) -> String {
  let pieces = split(s: path, delimiter: "/")
  fold(pieces, init:  "", f: (acc, piece) =>
    if acc == "" {
      piece
    } else {
      concat(acc, concat(".", piece))
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_classify(line: String) -> FloorPreparationLine {
  if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_phase_tag) {
    floor_preparation_classify_phase(line)
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_resolve_tag) {
    floor_preparation_classify_resolve(line)
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_shared_fill_tag) {
    floor_preparation_classify_claim(line, floor_preparation_shared_fill_tag)
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag) {
    floor_preparation_classify_claim(line, floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag)
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_witness_tag) {
    floor_preparation_classify_claim(line, floor_preparation_witness_tag)
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_pass_prefix) {
    VerdictLine { passed: true, function: floor_preparation_after_prefix(line, floor_preparation_pass_prefix) }
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, floor_preparation_fail_prefix) {
    VerdictLine { passed: false, function: floor_preparation_after_prefix(line, floor_preparation_fail_prefix) }
  } else if floor_preparation_starts_with(line, "[") {
    RefusedLine { text: line, cause: floor_preparation_unknown_tag_cause }
  } else {
    UntaggedLine { text: line }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_classify_phase(line: String) -> FloorPreparationLine {
  let fields = floor_preparation_fields_after(line, floor_preparation_phase_tag)
  match floor_preparation_field(fields, "phase") {
    Absent => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a [floor-phase] row with no phase= token; the fold cannot classify what it cannot name" }
    Present { value: phase } => PhaseLine { phase: phase, fields: fields }
  }
}

// `[resolve] <entry>: <ms>ms  (<n> modules, <m> resolved items in closure)` -- the per-entry-module
// resolution cost, which is preparation charged to ONE module. Producer:
// src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs:725 `resolve_timed`. The cost is the token after the `": "`
// separator, read with its unit required.
fn floor_preparation_classify_resolve(line: String) -> FloorPreparationLine {
  let rest = floor_preparation_after_prefix(line, concat(floor_preparation_resolve_tag, " "))
  let pieces = split(s: rest, delimiter: ": ")
  if pieces.length() < 2 {
    RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a [resolve] row without the `<entry>: <ms>ms` shape its producer prints" }
  } else {
    match pieces.first() {
      Absent => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a [resolve] row with no entry path" }
      Present { value: entry } =>
        match pieces.skip(n: 1).first() {
          Absent => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a [resolve] row with no cost token" }
          Present { value: cost_tail } =>
            match floor_preparation_tokens(cost_tail).first() {
              Absent => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a [resolve] row whose cost position is empty" }
              Present { value: cost_token } =>
                match floor_preparation_strip_suffix(cost_token, "ms") {
                  Absent => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a [resolve] row's cost carries no ms unit" }
                  Present { value: digits } =>
                    match floor_preparation_amount(key: "ms", text: digits) {
                      Amount { ms: n } => EntryResolveLine { entry: entry, ms: n }
                      MissingField { key: k } => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: concat("a [resolve] row carries no ", k) }
                      MalformedValue { key: k, text: v } => RefusedLine { text: line, cause: concat("a [resolve] row's ", concat(k, concat("=", concat(v, " is not a non-negative integer with an ms unit")))) }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_classify_claim(line: String, tag: String) -> FloorPreparationLine {
  let fields = floor_preparation_fields_after(line, tag)
  match floor_preparation_field(fields, "claim") {
    Present { value: claim } => ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: claim, fields: fields }
    Absent =>
      if tag == floor_preparation_witness_tag {
        // `[witness] <fn>: cpu=... ` puts the identity in the HEAD, not in a `claim=` field:
        // src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs:771 `witness_report_line` formats the function label
        // before the colon. The bare label carries no module -- which is exactly why a `[witness]` row
        // is keyed by the CURRENT ENTRY rather than by its own text.
        ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: "", fields: fields }
      } else {
        RefusedLine { text: line, cause: "a per-claim instrument row with no claim= identity" }
      }
  }
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE SPLIT
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

type FloorPreparationSplit
  = Split {
      preparation_ms: Millisecond,
      claim_ms: Millisecond,
      preparation_lines: Int,
      claim_lines: Int,
      uncosted_lines: Int,
      untagged_lines: Int,
      verdict_pass: Int,
      verdict_fail: Int,
      total_ms: Millisecond,
    }
  | Refused { text: String, cause: String }

// THE FOLD'S STATE. `current_entry` is the entry path the most recent `[resolve]` named -- the module
// the following per-claim rows belong to -- and `seen_resolve` distinguishes "no entry yet" from "the
// empty path", so a per-claim row printed before any resolve REFUSES instead of being attributed to a
// module nobody named.
type FloorPreparationFold {
  current_entry: String,
  seen_resolve: Bool,
  split: FloorPreparationSplit,
}

fn floor_preparation_empty_fold() -> FloorPreparationFold {
  FloorPreparationFold {
    current_entry: "",
    seen_resolve: false,
    split: Split { preparation_ms: floor_preparation_ms_zero(), claim_ms: floor_preparation_ms_zero(), preparation_lines: 0, claim_lines: 0, uncosted_lines: 0, untagged_lines: 0, verdict_pass: 0, verdict_fail: 0, total_ms: floor_preparation_ms_zero() },
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split(capture: List<String>) -> FloorPreparationSplit {
  fold(capture, init:  floor_preparation_empty_fold(), f: (acc, line) => floor_preparation_step(acc, line)).split
}

fn floor_preparation_step(acc: FloorPreparationFold, line: String) -> FloorPreparationFold {
  match acc.split {
    // A REFUSAL IS ABSORBING: once a line refuses, no later line turns it back into a reading. A
    // capture containing an unknown token has NO split, which is the whole point of the instrument.
    Refused { text: t, cause: c } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Refused { text: t, cause: c } }
    Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } =>
      match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
        RefusedLine { text: t, cause: why } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Refused { text: t, cause: why } }
        UntaggedLine { text: _ } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut + 1, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } }
        VerdictLine { passed: true, function: _ } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp + 1, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } }
        VerdictLine { passed: false, function: _ } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf + 1, total_ms: tm } }
        EntryResolveLine { entry: entry, ms: n } =>
          FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: entry, seen_resolve: true, split: Split { preparation_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(p, n), claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl + 1, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(tm, n) } }
        PhaseLine { phase: phase, fields: fields } => floor_preparation_phase_step(line: line, acc: acc, phase: phase, fields: fields)
        ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: fields } =>
          if acc.seen_resolve == false {
            FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Refused { text: line, cause: "a per-claim instrument row precedes any [resolve] entry; the fold will not invent the module it belongs to" } }
          } else {
            floor_preparation_claim_step(line: line, acc: acc, tag: tag, fields: fields)
          }
      }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_phase_step(line: String, acc: FloorPreparationFold, phase: String, fields: List<String>) -> FloorPreparationFold {
  match floor_preparation_phase_row(phase) {
    Absent => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: "an unknown [floor-phase] phase token; the split refuses rather than dropping a phase it cannot classify")
    Present { value: row } =>
      match row.class {
        PreparationCost =>
          if floor_preparation_state_not_completed(fields) {
            floor_preparation_uncosted(acc)
          } else {
            match floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, row.cost_field) {
              Amount { ms: n } => floor_preparation_add(side: PreparationCost, ms: n, acc: acc)
              MissingField { key: k } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a preparation phase row carries no ", k))
              MalformedValue { key: k, text: v } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a preparation phase row's ", concat(k, concat("=", concat(v, " is not a non-negative integer")))))
            }
          }
        ClaimExecutionCost =>
          if floor_preparation_state_not_completed(fields) {
            floor_preparation_uncosted(acc)
          } else {
            match floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, row.cost_field) {
              Amount { ms: n } => floor_preparation_add(side: ClaimExecutionCost, ms: n, acc: acc)
              MissingField { key: k } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a claim-side phase row carries no ", k))
              MalformedValue { key: k, text: v } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a claim-side phase row's ", concat(k, concat("=", concat(v, " is not a non-negative integer")))))
            }
          }
        NotCostBearing { reason: _ } => floor_preparation_uncosted(acc)
      }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_state_not_completed(fields: List<String>) -> Bool {
  match floor_preparation_field(fields, "state") {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: v } => v != "completed"
  }
}

// ONE INSTRUMENT ROW ABOUT ONE CLAIM, and the rows are NOT interchangeable. `[floor-shared-fill]`
// prints `marginal_cpu_ms` (what the claim itself owed, with the shared artifact already warm) beside
// `fill_cpu_ms` (what was owed to FILLING that artifact, which is preparation charged to this claim);
// the two halves sum to the claim's measured CPU, and each half belongs on its own side of the split
// (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/claim_execution.rs:150 "THE COST IS SPLIT, NEVER DROPPED").
// `[floor-reach-probe]` is printed IMMEDIATELY AFTER the fill row, under the same condition, and
// repeats THAT SAME `fill_cpu_ms` beside the reach judgement -- so it is classified uncosted. Counting
// it as preparation would bill every fill twice, inflating the preparation side in exactly the
// direction this node's premise is about; the executed witness
// `floor_preparation_reach_probe_row_is_not_billed_as_preparation` is what stops that reading.
// `[witness]` prints the claim's own `cpu=`, which is claim-side.
fn floor_preparation_claim_step(line: String, acc: FloorPreparationFold, tag: String, fields: List<String>) -> FloorPreparationFold {
  if tag == floor_preparation_witness_tag {
    match floor_preparation_ms_unit_field(fields, "cpu") {
      Amount { ms: n } => floor_preparation_add(side: ClaimExecutionCost, ms: n, acc: acc)
      MissingField { key: k } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a [witness] row carries no ", k))
      MalformedValue { key: k, text: v } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a [witness] row's ", concat(k, concat("=", concat(v, " is not a non-negative integer with an ms unit")))))
    }
  } else if tag == floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag {
    // The fill's OWN row was already billed by `[floor-shared-fill]`; this row's `fill_cpu_ms` is the
    // same quantity seen from the reach side. Uncosted by classification, counted, never silent.
    floor_preparation_uncosted(acc)
  } else {
    match floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "fill_cpu_ms") {
      Amount { ms: fill } =>
        match floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "marginal_cpu_ms") {
          Amount { ms: marginal } =>
            FloorPreparationFold {
              current_entry: acc.current_entry,
              seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve,
              split: floor_preparation_join_split(acc.split, preparation_delta: fill, claim_delta: marginal, preparation_lines: 1, claim_lines: 1),
            }
          MissingField { key: k } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a [floor-shared-fill] row carries no ", k))
          MalformedValue { key: k, text: v } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a [floor-shared-fill] row's ", concat(k, concat("=", concat(v, " is not a non-negative integer")))))
        }
      MissingField { key: k } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a per-claim fill row carries no ", k))
      MalformedValue { key: k, text: v } => floor_preparation_refuse(acc: acc, line: line, cause: concat("a per-claim fill row's ", concat(k, concat("=", concat(v, " is not a non-negative integer")))))
    }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_add(side: FloorPreparationCostClass, ms: Millisecond, acc: FloorPreparationFold) -> FloorPreparationFold {
  match side {
    PreparationCost => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: floor_preparation_join_split(acc.split, preparation_delta: ms, claim_delta: floor_preparation_ms_zero(), preparation_lines: 1, claim_lines: 0) }
    ClaimExecutionCost => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: floor_preparation_join_split(acc.split, preparation_delta: floor_preparation_ms_zero(), claim_delta: ms, preparation_lines: 0, claim_lines: 1) }
    NotCostBearing { reason: _ } => floor_preparation_uncosted(acc)
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_uncosted(acc: FloorPreparationFold) -> FloorPreparationFold {
  match acc.split {
    Refused { text: t, cause: c } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Refused { text: t, cause: c } }
    Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } => FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc + 1, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_refuse(acc: FloorPreparationFold, line: String, cause: String) -> FloorPreparationFold {
  FloorPreparationFold { current_entry: acc.current_entry, seen_resolve: acc.seen_resolve, split: Refused { text: line, cause: cause } }
}

// THE ONLY PLACE the split's numbers move, so conservation is a property of one function rather than of
// three call sites that could drift apart.
fn floor_preparation_join_split(split: FloorPreparationSplit, preparation_delta: Millisecond, claim_delta: Millisecond, preparation_lines: Int, claim_lines: Int) -> FloorPreparationSplit {
  match split {
    Refused { text: t, cause: c } => Refused { text: t, cause: c }
    Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } =>
      Split {
        preparation_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(p, preparation_delta),
        claim_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(cm, claim_delta),
        preparation_lines: pl + preparation_lines,
        claim_lines: cl + claim_lines,
        uncosted_lines: uc,
        untagged_lines: ut,
        verdict_pass: vp,
        verdict_fail: vf,
        total_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(
          floor_preparation_ms_add(tm, preparation_delta),
          claim_delta
        ),
      }
  }
}

// THE COST ONE LINE CONTRIBUTES, read from the same tables the fold uses. Two independent consumers
// need it: the conservation fold below, and the deletion-margin witness, which subtracts it from the
// total of the capture minus that line. If the fold charged a line anything other than what this
// reports, the two disagree and that witness goes red.
fn floor_preparation_line_ms(line: String) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
    RefusedLine { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    UntaggedLine { text: _ } => 0
    VerdictLine { passed: _, function: _ } => 0
    EntryResolveLine { entry: _, ms: n } => floor_preparation_ms_count(n)
    ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: fields } =>
      if tag == floor_preparation_witness_tag {
        floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_unit_field(fields, "cpu"))
      } else if tag == floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag {
        0
      } else {
        floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "fill_cpu_ms")) + floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "marginal_cpu_ms"))
      }
    PhaseLine { phase: phase, fields: fields } =>
      match floor_preparation_phase_row(phase) {
        Absent => 0
        Present { value: row } =>
          if floor_preparation_state_not_completed(fields) {
            0
          } else {
            match row.class {
              PreparationCost => floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, row.cost_field))
              ClaimExecutionCost => floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, row.cost_field))
              NotCostBearing { reason: _ } => 0
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

// THE GRAND TOTAL, folded independently of the split's accumulator. The conservation witness compares
// the two: a line dropped, double-counted or filed under the wrong class makes them disagree.
fn floor_preparation_total_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) => acc + floor_preparation_line_ms(line))
}

fn floor_preparation_lines_are_closed(capture: List<String>) -> Bool {
  fold(capture, init:  true, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      RefusedLine { text: _, cause: _ } => false
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_refusal(capture: List<String>) -> Optional<String> {
  fold(capture, init:  none, f: (acc, line) =>
    match acc {
      Present { value: v } => Present { value: v }
      Absent =>
        match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
          RefusedLine { text: _, cause: why } => Present { value: why }
          _ => none
        }
    })
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE MODULE-GRAIN ATTRIBUTION. Phase rows name no module -- they are whole-run preparation -- and are
// reported separately rather than attributed to a module they do not belong to. Entry-resolve rows name
// their own entry; per-claim rows are attributed to the entry whose block they were printed under,
// which is the printer's fact and is therefore THREADED, not inferred from the row's own text.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

type FloorPreparationModuleCost {
  module: String,
  preparation_ms: Millisecond,
  claim_ms: Millisecond,
  lines: Int,
}

type FloorPreparationAttribution
  = Attributed { modules: List<FloorPreparationModuleCost>, module_count: Int, top_module: String, top_ms: Millisecond }
  | Unattributed {}

// THE ENTRY PATHS THE RUN NAMED, one per resolved entry.
fn floor_preparation_entry_paths(capture: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  let pushed = fold(capture, init:  [], f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      EntryResolveLine { entry: entry, ms: _ } => concat([entry], acc)
      _ => acc
    })
  floor_preparation_reverse(pushed)
}

fn floor_preparation_module_keys(capture: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  distinct_by_key(xs: floor_preparation_entry_paths(capture), key: fn(p) { floor_preparation_module_of_path(p) })
}

// THE COST ROW FOR ONE MODULE, folded with the entry currently in force. A per-claim row is charged to
// a module ONLY while that module's entry is in force, so a fold that ignored the threading would
// charge every claim to every module and the attribution witness would go red on the spot.
fn floor_preparation_module_cost(target_path: String, capture: List<String>) -> FloorPreparationModuleCost {
  let target = floor_preparation_module_of_path(target_path)
  fold(
    capture, init: FloorPreparationModuleCost { module: target, preparation_ms: floor_preparation_ms_zero(), claim_ms: floor_preparation_ms_zero(), lines: 0 },
    f: (acc, line) => floor_preparation_module_step(acc: acc, in_force: floor_preparation_module_of_path(target_path), line: line)
  )
}

fn floor_preparation_module_step(acc: FloorPreparationModuleCost, in_force: String, line: String) -> FloorPreparationModuleCost {
  match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
    EntryResolveLine { entry: entry, ms: n } =>
      if floor_preparation_module_of_path(entry) != acc.module {
        acc
      } else {
        FloorPreparationModuleCost { module: acc.module, preparation_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(acc.preparation_ms, n), claim_ms: acc.claim_ms, lines: acc.lines + 1 }
      }
    ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: fields } =>
      if in_force != acc.module {
        acc
      } else if tag == floor_preparation_witness_tag {
        match floor_preparation_ms_unit_field(fields, "cpu") {
          Amount { ms: n } => FloorPreparationModuleCost { module: acc.module, preparation_ms: acc.preparation_ms, claim_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(acc.claim_ms, n), lines: acc.lines + 1 }
          _ => acc
        }
      } else if tag == floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag {
        acc
      } else {
        match floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "fill_cpu_ms") {
          Amount { ms: fill } =>
            match floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "marginal_cpu_ms") {
              Amount { ms: marginal } => FloorPreparationModuleCost { module: acc.module, preparation_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(acc.preparation_ms, fill), claim_ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(acc.claim_ms, marginal), lines: acc.lines + 1 }
              _ => acc
            }
          _ => acc
        }
      }
    _ => acc
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_attribution(capture: List<String>) -> FloorPreparationAttribution {
  let paths = floor_preparation_entry_paths(capture)
  let keys = distinct_by_key(xs: paths, key: fn(p) { floor_preparation_module_of_path(p) })
  if length(xs: keys) == 0 {
    Unattributed {}
  } else {
    let costs = fold(keys, init:  [], f: (acc, key) => concat([floor_preparation_module_cost(key, capture)], acc))
    match floor_preparation_max(costs) {
      Absent => Unattributed {}
      Present { value: top } => Attributed { modules: floor_preparation_reverse(costs), module_count: floor_preparation_count(costs), top_module: top.module, top_ms: floor_preparation_module_total(top) }
    }
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_module_total(row: FloorPreparationModuleCost) -> Millisecond {
  floor_preparation_ms_add(row.preparation_ms, row.claim_ms)
}

fn floor_preparation_max(rows: List<FloorPreparationModuleCost>) -> Optional<FloorPreparationModuleCost> {
  fold(rows, init:  none, f: (acc, row) =>
    match acc {
      Absent => Present { value: row }
      Present { value: best } => if floor_preparation_ms_count(floor_preparation_module_total(row)) > floor_preparation_ms_count(floor_preparation_module_total(best)) { Present { value: row } } else { Present { value: best } }
    })
}

// THE SUM OVER THE MODULE TABLE of the entry-resolve and per-claim costs. It must equal the split's own
// total MINUS the phase rows' contribution -- an equality the attribution witness checks, because a
// row that reached the split but not the module table (or the reverse) is how a module-grain report
// silently lies.
fn floor_preparation_attributed_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_attribution(capture) {
    Unattributed {} => 0
    Attributed { modules: rows, module_count: _, top_module: _, top_ms: _ } =>
      fold(rows, init:  0, f: (acc, row) => acc + floor_preparation_ms_count(floor_preparation_module_total(row)))
  }
}

// THE PHASE ROWS ALONE, which is what the split's total exceeds the module table by.
fn floor_preparation_phase_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      PhaseLine { phase: _, fields: _ } => acc + floor_preparation_line_ms(line)
      _ => acc
    })
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE SCALE SPLIT OF THE PREPARATION SIDE -- the number the affordability decision turns on.
// Folded INDEPENDENTLY of the split's accumulator (the same discipline as `total_ms`), and the
// witness `floor_preparation_preparation_sides_partition_by_scale` requires the two halves to
// sum to the split's own preparation total, so an unclassified phase row cannot hide.
//
// WHOLE-TREE preparation recurs no matter what the diff touches, so nothing but reusing
// resolved-module and reach-probe results ACROSS RUNS stops paying it. ENTRY-CLOSURE preparation
// is sized by the run's entries -- `scope=entry-closure-union`, `sources=`, the per-entry
// `[resolve]` rows -- so scoping preparation to a diff's closure cuts it directly. Read the two
// numbers off a required-shaped run and the choice between the roadmap's two constructions is
// arithmetic; read only the total and it is a preference.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn floor_preparation_whole_tree_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      PhaseLine { phase: phase, fields: fields } =>
        match floor_preparation_phase_row(phase) {
          Present { value: row } =>
            match row.scale {
              WholeTreeScale => acc + floor_preparation_line_ms(line)
              EntryClosureScale => acc
            }
          Absent => acc
        }
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_entry_scoped_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      PhaseLine { phase: phase, fields: fields } =>
        match floor_preparation_phase_row(phase) {
          Present { value: row } =>
            match row.scale {
              EntryClosureScale => acc + floor_preparation_line_ms(line)
              WholeTreeScale => acc
            }
          Absent => acc
        }
      // THE PER-ENTRY RESOLUTION IS ENTRY-SCOPED BY DEFINITION: one entry, one cost, charged to
      // that module. It is also the only preparation row that is module-grain on its own face.
      EntryResolveLine { entry: _, ms: n } => acc + floor_preparation_ms_count(n)
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_phase_row_count(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      PhaseLine { phase: _, fields: _ } => acc + 1
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_claim_row_count(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      ClaimLine { tag: _, claim: _, fields: _ } => acc + 1
      _ => acc
    })
}

// THE REACH-PROBE FILLS, as the sum of `fill_cpu_ms` over the probe rows ONLY. This is the number that
// makes the probe row's classification causal rather than merely consistent: were the probe row counted
// as preparation, the split's total would exceed the conservation total by exactly this much.
fn floor_preparation_probe_fill_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: fields } =>
        if tag == floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag {
          acc + floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "fill_cpu_ms"))
        } else {
          acc
        }
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_fill_row_count(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: _ } => if tag == floor_preparation_shared_fill_tag { acc + 1 } else { acc }
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_probe_row_count(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: _ } => if tag == floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag { acc + 1 } else { acc }
      _ => acc
    })
}

// THE COSTED LINE AT AN INDEX, which the deletion-margin check uses to name the line it removed.
type FloorPreparationScan {
  i: Int,
  found: String,
}

fn floor_preparation_line_at(capture: List<String>, index: Int) -> String {
  let pair = fold(capture, init:  FloorPreparationScan { i: 0, found: "" }, f: (acc, line) =>
    if acc.i == index {
      FloorPreparationScan { i: acc.i + 1, found: line }
    } else {
      FloorPreparationScan { i: acc.i + 1, found: acc.found }
    })
  pair.found
}

type FloorPreparationDrop {
  i: Int,
  kept: List<String>,
}

fn floor_preparation_kept(state: FloorPreparationDrop) -> List<String> {
  floor_preparation_reverse(state.kept)
}

fn floor_preparation_without_index(capture: List<String>, index: Int) -> List<String> {
  let state = fold(capture, init:  FloorPreparationDrop { i: 0, kept: [] }, f: (acc, line) =>
    if acc.i == index {
      FloorPreparationDrop { i: acc.i + 1, kept: acc.kept }
    } else {
      FloorPreparationDrop { i: acc.i + 1, kept: concat([line], acc.kept) }
    })
  floor_preparation_kept(state)
}

// THE DELETION MARGIN, OVER EVERY LINE THAT CARRIES A COST. For each, the total of the capture MINUS
// that line must fall by exactly what that line reports. A fold that charged a line something other than
// what `floor_preparation_line_ms` reports, or that read a figure from anywhere but the lines, cannot
// satisfy this for every costed line at once.
fn floor_preparation_deletion_margin_holds(capture: List<String>) -> Bool {
  let whole = floor_preparation_total_ms(capture)
  let n = length(xs: capture)
  let state = fold(capture, init:  FloorPreparationMargin { i: 0, ok: true, costed: 0 }, f: (acc, line) =>
    if floor_preparation_line_ms(line) == 0 {
      FloorPreparationMargin { i: acc.i + 1, ok: acc.ok, costed: acc.costed }
    } else {
      let without = floor_preparation_without_index(capture, acc.i)
      FloorPreparationMargin {
        i: acc.i + 1,
        ok: acc.ok && floor_preparation_total_ms(without) == whole - floor_preparation_line_ms(line),
        costed: acc.costed + 1,
      }
    })
  floor_preparation_margin_ok(state)
}

type FloorPreparationMargin {
  i: Int,
  ok: Bool,
  costed: Int,
}

fn floor_preparation_margin_ok(state: FloorPreparationMargin) -> Bool {
  state.ok && state.costed > 0 && state.i == length(xs: floor_preparation_capture())
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// READERS THE CLAIMS MODULE USES. Every one answers for ONE property and returns a plain value, so the
// claims module never matches a variant of this file's enums: the readings are the surface, and a
// refused capture reads as `..._is_refused` true with zeroes beside it rather than as a silent zero.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn floor_preparation_split_is_refused(capture: List<String>) -> Bool {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => true
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: _ } => false
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_total_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: tm } => floor_preparation_ms_count(tm)
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_preparation_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: _ } => floor_preparation_ms_count(p)
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_claim_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: _ } => floor_preparation_ms_count(cm)
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_preparation_lines(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: _ } => pl
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_claim_lines(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: _ } => cl
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_pass(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: _, total_ms: _ } => vp
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_fail(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
    Refused { text: _, cause: _ } => 0
    Split { preparation_ms: _, claim_ms: _, preparation_lines: _, claim_lines: _, uncosted_lines: _, untagged_lines: _, verdict_pass: _, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: _ } => vf
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_attribution_is_unattributed(capture: List<String>) -> Bool {
  match floor_preparation_attribution(capture) {
    Unattributed {} => true
    Attributed { modules: _, module_count: _, top_module: _, top_ms: _ } => false
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_attribution_all_rows_have_lines(capture: List<String>) -> Bool {
  match floor_preparation_attribution(capture) {
    Unattributed {} => false
    Attributed { modules: rows, module_count: _, top_module: _, top_ms: _ } =>
      fold(rows, init:  true, f: (acc, row) => acc && row.lines > 0)
  }
}

// THE FILL SUM OVER THE `[floor-shared-fill]` ROWS -- the same quantity the probe rows report, and the
// equality the causality claim needs.
fn floor_preparation_fill_fill_ms(capture: List<String>) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: fields } =>
        if tag == floor_preparation_shared_fill_tag {
          acc + floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "fill_cpu_ms"))
        } else {
          acc
        }
      _ => acc
    })
}

// THE RESOLVE-ROW / MODULE-ROW AGREEMENT, checked off the capture with its own threading so it tests
// the module table's bookkeeping instead of restating it. For every module row: the table's preparation
// must equal that entry's `[resolve]` cost plus the fills charged to it while its entry was in force.
fn floor_preparation_resolve_rows_match_their_module_rows(capture: List<String>) -> Bool {
  match floor_preparation_attribution(capture) {
    Unattributed {} => false
    Attributed { modules: rows, module_count: _, top_module: _, top_ms: _ } =>
      fold(rows, init:  true, f: (acc, row) =>
        acc && floor_preparation_ms_count(row.preparation_ms) == floor_preparation_module_resolve_ms(capture, row.module) + floor_preparation_module_fill_ms(capture, row.module))
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_module_resolve_ms(capture: List<String>, module: String) -> Int {
  fold(capture, init:  0, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      EntryResolveLine { entry: entry, ms: n } => if floor_preparation_module_of_path(entry) == module { acc + floor_preparation_ms_count(n) } else { acc }
      _ => acc
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_module_fill_ms(capture: List<String>, module: String) -> Int {
  let state = fold(capture, init:  FloorPreparationInForce { entry: "", ms: floor_preparation_ms_zero() }, f: (acc, line) =>
    match floor_preparation_classify(line) {
      EntryResolveLine { entry: entry, ms: _ } => FloorPreparationInForce { entry: floor_preparation_module_of_path(entry), ms: acc.ms }
      ClaimLine { tag: tag, claim: _, fields: fields } =>
        if acc.entry != module || tag == floor_preparation_reach_probe_tag || tag == floor_preparation_witness_tag {
          acc
        } else {
          FloorPreparationInForce { entry: acc.entry, ms: floor_preparation_ms_add(acc.ms, floor_preparation_ms_of(floor_preparation_amount_ms(floor_preparation_ms_field(fields, "fill_cpu_ms")))) }
        }
      _ => acc
    })
  floor_preparation_ms_count(state.ms)
}

type FloorPreparationInForce {
  entry: String,
  ms: Millisecond,
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE ENTRY POINT
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// THE REPORT PROTOCOL. `gunbc run --function` has no channel for a successful String result (the
// host maps a verdict to an exit code and only ProcessExit carries one -- an earliest_unjustified_
// boundary taken upward as a platform finding, not fixed here). The runner's report leg therefore
// READS its success off the printed line, and that would be unverifiable hope unless a real refusal
// could not possibly read as a report. It cannot: every line the report emits -- report, refusal,
// or empty-population -- carries the model-rendered sentinel below, and a line is classified
// REPORT_READ only if it matches the closed report grammar, carries the sentinel verbatim, and
// carries neither the refusal marker nor the empty-population marker. "The report says X" and "I
// could not read a report" are different verdicts with different text, never the same PASS.
data floor_preparation_report_sentinel: String = "protocol=floor-preparation-split-v1"

data floor_preparation_report_prefix: String = "floor-preparation-split "

data floor_preparation_report_refusal_marker: String = "REFUSED:"

data floor_preparation_report_empty_marker: String = "population=EMPTY"

fn floor_preparation_report_is_wellformed(line: String) -> Bool {
  floor_preparation_starts_with(text: line, prefix: floor_preparation_report_prefix)
    && floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: floor_preparation_report_sentinel)
    && floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: " preparation_ms=")
    && floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: " total_ms=")
    && floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: " pass=")
    && !floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: floor_preparation_report_refusal_marker)
    && !floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: floor_preparation_report_empty_marker)
}

fn floor_preparation_classify_report_line(line: String) -> String {
  if !floor_preparation_starts_with(text: line, prefix: floor_preparation_report_prefix) {
    "UNRECOGNISED_OUTPUT"
  } else if floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: floor_preparation_report_refusal_marker) {
    "REFUSAL_NOT_A_REPORT"
  } else if floor_preparation_contains(haystack: line, needle: floor_preparation_report_empty_marker) {
    "POPULATION_EMPTY_NOT_A_REPORT"
  } else if floor_preparation_report_is_wellformed(line: line) {
    "REPORT_READ"
  } else {
    "UNRECOGNISED_OUTPUT"
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_split_report() -> String {
  let capture = floor_preparation_capture()
  if length(xs: capture) == 0 {
    join([concat(floor_preparation_report_prefix, "population=EMPTY protocol="), floor_preparation_report_sentinel, " instrument=", floor_preparation_capture_provenance(), " -- nothing was measured and no dominance is claimed"], "")
  } else {
    match floor_preparation_split(capture) {
      Refused { text: t, cause: c } =>
        join(
          [
            concat(floor_preparation_report_prefix, "REFUSED: ", floor_preparation_report_sentinel, " " ),
            c,
            " || first_token=",
            floor_preparation_head(t),
            " || capture_lines=",
            to_string(length(xs: capture)),
            " || instrument=",
            floor_preparation_capture_provenance(),
          ],
          ""
        )
      Split { preparation_ms: p, claim_ms: cm, preparation_lines: pl, claim_lines: cl, uncosted_lines: uc, untagged_lines: ut, verdict_pass: vp, verdict_fail: vf, total_ms: tm } =>
        match floor_preparation_attribution(capture) {
          Unattributed {} => join([floor_preparation_split_line(p, cm, pl, cl, uc, ut, vp, vf, tm), " modules=none"], "")
          Attributed { modules: rows, module_count: mc, top_module: top, top_ms: top_ms } =>
            join(
              [
                floor_preparation_split_line(p, cm, pl, cl, uc, ut, vp, vf, tm),
                " instrument=",
                floor_preparation_capture_provenance(),
                " phase_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_phase_ms(capture)),
                " whole_tree_preparation_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_whole_tree_ms(capture)),
                " entry_scoped_preparation_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_entry_scoped_ms(capture)),
                " attributed_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_attributed_ms(capture)),
                " modules=",
                to_string(mc),
                " top_module=",
                top,
                " top_module_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_ms_count(top_ms)),
                " module_table=",
                floor_preparation_module_table(rows),
                " untrimmed_total_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_untrimmed_total_ms()),
                " untrimmed_preparation_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_untrimmed_preparation_ms()),
                " untrimmed_claim_ms=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_untrimmed_claim_ms()),
                " untrimmed_fail=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_untrimmed_verdict_fail()),
                " untrimmed_untagged_lines=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_untrimmed_untagged_lines()),
                " enrolled_claims=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_requested_row_count()),
                " graded_claims=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_graded_row_count()),
                " excluded_claims=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_excluded_row_count()),
                " excluded_refused=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_excluded_with_cause(floor_preparation_cause_refused)),
                " excluded_unobserved=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_excluded_with_cause(floor_preparation_cause_unobserved)),
                " excluded_no_verdict_line=",
                to_string(floor_preparation_excluded_with_cause(floor_preparation_cause_no_verdict)),
                " census_is_honest=",
                floor_preparation_yes_no(floor_preparation_census_is_honest()),
                " untrimmed_covers_graded=",
                floor_preparation_yes_no(floor_preparation_untrimmed_covers_the_graded_population()),
                " enrolled_modules=",
                to_string(length(xs: floor_preparation_requested_modules())),
                " ask=",
                floor_preparation_ask(),
              ],
              ""
            )
        }
    }
  }
}

// Duration carries the Millisecond unit all the way to the printer; the digit rendering
// (review 97819) happens HERE, at the printing boundary, not in callers. Line and verdict
// counts stay Int: they are counts, not durations.
fn floor_preparation_split_line(preparation_ms: Millisecond, claim_ms: Millisecond, preparation_lines: Int, claim_lines: Int, uncosted_lines: Int, untagged_lines: Int, verdict_pass: Int, verdict_fail: Int, total_ms: Millisecond) -> String {
  join(
    [
      concat(floor_preparation_report_prefix, "preparation_ms="),
      to_string(floor_preparation_ms_count(preparation_ms)),
      " claim_ms=",
      to_string(floor_preparation_ms_count(claim_ms)),
      " total_ms=",
      to_string(floor_preparation_ms_count(total_ms)),
      " preparation_lines=",
      to_string(preparation_lines),
      " claim_lines=",
      to_string(claim_lines),
      " uncosted_lines=",
      to_string(uncosted_lines),
      " untagged_lines=",
      to_string(untagged_lines),
      " pass=",
      to_string(verdict_pass),
      " fail=",
      to_string(verdict_fail),
    ],
    ""
  )
}

fn floor_preparation_module_table(rows: List<FloorPreparationModuleCost>) -> String {
  fold(rows, init:  "", f: (acc, row) =>
    if acc == "" {
      floor_preparation_module_cell(row)
    } else {
      concat(acc, concat(" ; ", floor_preparation_module_cell(row)))
    })
}

fn floor_preparation_module_cell(row: FloorPreparationModuleCost) -> String {
  join([row.module, " preparation=", to_string(floor_preparation_ms_count(row.preparation_ms)), " claim=", to_string(floor_preparation_ms_count(row.claim_ms)), " lines=", to_string(row.lines)], "")
}

fn floor_preparation_head(text: String) -> String {
  match floor_preparation_tokens(text).first() {
    Present { value: head } => head
    Absent => ""
  }
}

fn floor_preparation_ask() -> String {
  concat(
    "gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/workflow/floor_preparation_capture_runner.dag --function floor_preparation_capture_run",
    "   (the modelled runner: legs spawn through shell.Exec.RunArgv inside heavy-slot; it prints per-leg receipts with real exit statuses, classifies the report line REPORT_READ/REFUSAL_NOT_A_REPORT, and refuses unless every enrolled claim printed its own PASS line)"
  )
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE RUNNER, MODELLED. There is no shell. The whole capture process lives in
// `v2.workflow.floor_preparation_capture_runner`: the step list is data there, each leg spawns the
// pinned binaries through the declared shell-transport service (shell.Exec.RunArgv), the heavy slot
// is the outermost argv word (env HEAVY_OWNER=<session> heavy-slot ...), and artifacts are written
// with the Filesystem.Write effect. The claims module refuses when a declared step has no emission
// site in the same module, and when the leg argv is not the model-rendered argv. The population
// file is likewise modelled -- its rows are data here, and the committed text file is a rendering
// of them refused by a claim whenever it disagrees with the model.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


// THE POPULATION IS MODEL DATA. One authoritative declaration of which claims the floor fold
// measures, at entry grain -- enrolled as candidates, and enrolled as extras so a refusal stays
// in the artifact with its cause. The committed txt file is a PROJECTION of these rows; claim
// floor_preparation_the_population_is_the_models_rendering refuses if the file (minus comment
// lines) ever disagrees with the rendering below, and the capture runner re-checks the same
// equality before any leg spawns.
type FloorPreparationPopulationKind =
  Candidate
  | Extra

type FloorPreparationPopulationRow {
  kind: FloorPreparationPopulationKind,
  entry: String,
  claim: String,
}

data floor_preparation_population_model_rows: List<FloorPreparationPopulationRow> = [
